{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-11-14T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Dawn's first light is reflected on the frozen surface of Abraham Lake, framed by Rocky Mountains peaks in western Canada. In winter, this picturesque lake in Alberta is famous for its frozen bubbles of methane gas, trapped beneath the ice. Strong winds keep the surface clear of snow, offering winter-long views. Come spring, when the ice thaws, the gas escapes into the atmosphere.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AbrahamCanada_ROW4975668347_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AbrahamCanada_ROW4975668347_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Abraham Lake in Alberta, Canada","Copyright":"© Guang Cao/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261113_AbrahamCanada\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Abraham+Lake+Alberta&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261113_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261113_AbrahamCanada"},"Ssd":"20261113","Name":"AbrahamCanada","Market":"ROW","Hash":"4975668347","FullDateString":"Nov 13, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Just north of Moab, Utah, the high-desert park is home to more than 2,000 natural sandstone arches—the densest concentration of arches in the world. Today's image, North Window, is one of the best-known formations in the park's Windows Section, where towering fins, openings and sculpted sandstone create a landscape that looks almost architectural.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NorthWindow_ROW5709754561_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NorthWindow_ROW5709754561_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"North Window, Arches National Park, Moab, Utah, USA","Copyright":"© lightphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261112_NorthWindow\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Arches+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261112_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261112_NorthWindow"},"Ssd":"20261112","Name":"NorthWindow","Market":"ROW","Hash":"5709754561","FullDateString":"Nov 12, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Atlantic Forest is one of the world's great biodiversity hotspots, stretching along much of Brazil's Atlantic coast and into Argentina and Paraguay. Its landscape includes tropical and subtropical forests, mangroves and coastal habitats, providing a home for around 20,000 plant species and an extraordinary variety of wildlife, including jaguars and golden lion tamarins. Much of the forest has disappeared over the centuries, but it continues to play an important role in storing carbon and providing fresh water for millions of people across the region.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Atlantica_ROW8494593651_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Atlantica_ROW8494593651_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"The Atlantic Forest, Brazil","Copyright":"© FG Trade/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261111_Atlantica\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Atlantic+Forest+Brazil&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261111_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261111_Atlantica"},"Ssd":"20261111","Name":"Atlantica","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8494593651","FullDateString":"Nov 11, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"From above, Rose Island looks like a brushstroke of green surrounded by every shade of blue. Just five kilometres east of Paradise Island in The Bahamas, this slender cay trades busy roads and city blocks for sandy shores, shallow waters and an inland lagoon. Its peaceful appearance comes with a touch of movie drama. Rose Island was used as a filming location for the 1965 James Bond adventure 'Thunderball', including the explosive destruction of the Disco Volante.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RoseIsland_ROW8217613794_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RoseIsland_ROW8217613794_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Aerial view of Rose Island, The Bahamas","Copyright":"© Abstract Aerial Art/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261110_RoseIsland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Rose+Island+Bahamas&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261110_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261110_RoseIsland"},"Ssd":"20261110","Name":"RoseIsland","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8217613794","FullDateString":"Nov 10, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Cross the Guadalquivir River in Seville, the capital of Spain's Andalusia region, and the city's rhythm seems to change. On the other side lies Triana, a colourful neighbourhood where ceramics, flamenco and local traditions are woven into everyday life. Since the 19th century, the Isabel II Bridge, also known as the Triana Bridge, has connected the neighbourhood to Seville's historic centre.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.TrianaSpain_ROW7617415595_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.TrianaSpain_ROW7617415595_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Historic district of Triana, Seville, Spain","Copyright":"© Andrzej Rostek/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261109_TrianaSpain\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Seville+Spain&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261109_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261109_TrianaSpain"},"Ssd":"20261109","Name":"TrianaSpain","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7617415595","FullDateString":"Nov 9, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Ebro Delta in Catalonia is one of Spain's most rewarding places to see flamingos. These unmistakable birds can be spotted throughout the year, often gathering in the delta's shallow lagoons, salt pans and coastal waters. Their long legs let them wade through the water while feeding, while their pink colouring comes from pigments found in their diet. With wetlands, rice fields, beaches and the Mediterranean all meeting here, the delta provides an important home for both resident and migratory birds. Flamingos have become one of its most recognisable sights, adding a splash of colour to this remarkable landscape.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DeltaEbro_ROW7248981899_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DeltaEbro_ROW7248981899_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Flamingos in Ebro Delta Natural Park, Catalonia, Spain","Copyright":"© mafrmcfa/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261108_DeltaEbro\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ebro+Delta+Natural+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261108_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261108_DeltaEbro"},"Ssd":"20261108","Name":"DeltaEbro","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7248981899","FullDateString":"Nov 8, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Bison are among the largest land mammals in the world, capable of weighing up to 900 kilograms and reaching speeds of 65 kilometres per hour despite their massive size. Despite often being called a buffalo, the American bison is not one of the true buffaloes, which are native to Africa and Asia. Its scientific name, Bison bison, leaves little room for confusion.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DakotaBison_ROW7172064410_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DakotaBison_ROW7172064410_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"A bison in the grasslands of Theodore Roosevelt National Park, North Dakota, USA","Copyright":"© Tandem Stock/Adobe Stock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261107_DakotaBison\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=American+bison&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261107_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261107_DakotaBison"},"Ssd":"20261107","Name":"DakotaBison","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7172064410","FullDateString":"Nov 7, jjjj"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Off the coast of Kvaløya in Troms, Northern Norway, humpback whales move through the cold Arctic waters in search of a proper feast. They visit this region during the winter months, following migrating herring into the fjords. Humpbacks are famous for bubble-net feeding, a remarkable hunting technique in which whales blow rings of bubbles to corral fish before lunging upwards, open-mouthed, to catch their prey. In today's image, a humpback slips beneath the icy waves under a glowing pastel sky, capturing a moment of tranquility in Norway's wild north.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Megaptera_ROW6602236016_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Megaptera_ROW6602236016_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Diving humpback whale, Kvaloya, Troms, Northern Norway","Copyright":"© Espen Bergersen/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261120_Megaptera\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=humpback+whales&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261120_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261120_Megaptera"},"Ssd":"20261120","Name":"Megaptera","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6602236016","FullDateString":"Nov 20, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Step into this peaceful redwood forest in Victoria, Australia, and the outside world can suddenly feel very far away. Coast redwoods (Sequoia sempervirens) tower overhead, forming a leafy canopy above the forest floor. These impressive trees have grown into one of the region's most distinctive woodland sights. With their tall trunks, deep green foliage and tranquil surroundings, the redwoods create an inviting place to wander, slow down and enjoy the quiet beauty of the forest.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MelbourneRedwoods_ROW6372871248_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MelbourneRedwoods_ROW6372871248_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Coast redwoods near Melbourne, Victoria, Australia","Copyright":"© James Yu/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261119_MelbourneRedwoods\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sequoia+sempervirens&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261119_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261119_MelbourneRedwoods"},"Ssd":"20261119","Name":"MelbourneRedwoods","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6372871248","FullDateString":"Nov 19, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"These barn owls, bathed in evening light, are waiting for the hunt to begin. As night falls, these birds of prey swoop into action, listening for tiny movements in grass or leaves made by mice and voles. Their heart-shaped faces help funnel sound into some of the sharpest ears in the animal kingdom. This allows them to locate their prey with pinpoint precision in the dark before swooping silently, their soft feathers muffling their approach. In autumn, young barn owls strike out to find their own territories. As the nights grow longer, you might spot them earlier in the evening, gliding over fields in search of supper.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BarnOwlsUnite_ROW6271604820_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BarnOwlsUnite_ROW6271604820_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Pair of barn owls","Copyright":"© Zahoor Salmi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261118_BarnOwlsUnite\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Barn+owl&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261118_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261118_BarnOwlsUnite"},"Ssd":"20261118","Name":"BarnOwlsUnite","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6271604820","FullDateString":"Nov 18, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Sometimes, the best way to clear your head is to step outside. Today's image features the Trail of the Cedars, part of more than 1,100 kilometres of hiking trails in Glacier National Park, Montana, in the northwestern USA. Its 1.4-kilometre loop includes a raised boardwalk that cuts a path through western red cedar and hemlock trees. The park boasts routes for all abilities, taking in alpine lakes, wildflower meadows, mountain passes and wilderness stretching to the Canadian border.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.TrailCedars_ROW6107816047_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.TrailCedars_ROW6107816047_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Trail of the Cedars, Glacier National Park, Montana, USA","Copyright":"© DBushue Photography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261117_TrailCedars\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Trail+of+the+Cedars&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261117_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261117_TrailCedars"},"Ssd":"20261117","Name":"TrailCedars","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6107816047","FullDateString":"Nov 17, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Incredible views and rock-solid foundations are part of the charm of these ancient dwellings, set into the cliffside in New Mexico, USA. Nomads had long used the natural caves above Cliff Dweller Creek as temporary shelter, but it was the Native American Mogollon people who made them their home. Archaeologists believe they created dozens of rooms inside five alcoves in the 1270s and 1280s. Up to 15 families lived here at any one time, raising children, making pottery and overlooking the fertile Gila River valley where they grew crops and hunted wildlife. For reasons unknown, the Mogollon people moved on around 1300, leaving behind one of the American Southwest's most important archaeological sites.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GilaCliff_ROW5960011422_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GilaCliff_ROW5960011422_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Gila Cliff Dwellings National Monument, New Mexico, USA","Copyright":"© Chiara Salvadori/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261116_GilaCliff\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Gila+Cliff+Dwellings+National+Monument&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261116_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261116_GilaCliff"},"Ssd":"20261116","Name":"GilaCliff","Market":"ROW","Hash":"5960011422","FullDateString":"Nov 16, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As colder weather sets in, ice crystals form on the leaves of evergreen shrubs, like this azalea. Long gone are the pinks, orange and yellows of their spring blooms, but a new colourful display awaits, as their green leaves turn shades of red and purple. For the plants, the new pigments protect their leaves as temperatures drop, but for gardeners, they create a vibrant autumnal display, framed in white frost. When spring arrives, new growth will restore the shrub's green leaves, and the colourful cycle begins anew.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FirstFrost_ROW5798320108_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FirstFrost_ROW5798320108_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Frozen azalea with red leaves","Copyright":"© avoferten/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261115_FirstFrost\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=azaleas&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261115_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261115_FirstFrost"},"Ssd":"20261115","Name":"FirstFrost","Market":"ROW","Hash":"5798320108","FullDateString":"Nov 15, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Welcome to Hong Kong, home to the world's largest collection of skyscrapers. Those pictured here tower above Victoria Harbour, whose deep waters allowed the island to develop as a busy trading port. Ships carrying tea, silk and other goods have passed through since the 1840s, but growth rocketed in the decades after World War II, fueling a construction boom. With little flat land available between the harbour and the hills, developers had to build upwards, creating this distinctive skyline. In 2026, Hong Kong has 569 buildings at least 150 metres tall high — more than any other city.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BlueHK_ROW5600938316_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BlueHK_ROW5600938316_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Victoria Harbour, Hong Kong, China","Copyright":"© Juan Romero/Cavan Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261114_BlueHK\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Victoria+Harbour+Hong+Kong&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261114_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261114_BlueHK"},"Ssd":"20261114","Name":"BlueHK","Market":"ROW","Hash":"5600938316","FullDateString":"Nov 14, jjjj"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"Beeld van die dag","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD_LEARN_MORE":"Kom meer te wete","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_FACT":"Kitsfeit:","LOC_HOMEPAGE_GALLERY_CARD_TITLE":"Onlangse tuisbladbeelde","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_GALLERY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"Tuisbladbeeld vir {0}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_TITLE":"Op hierdie dag in geskiedenis","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"Op hierdie dag in {0}, {1}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_SHARE_TOOLTIP":"Deel vandag se Bing-tuisblad","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERDOWNLOAD_TOOLTIP":"Laai hierdie beeld af. Hierdie beeld kan slegs as muurpapier gebruik word.","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERNOTAVAILABLE":"Hierdie beeld kan nie as muurpapier afgelaai word nie.","LOC_HOMEPAGE_INFO_TEXT":"Inligting","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK":"https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2127455","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK_TEXT":"Kry die Bing-muurpapiertoepassing","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_TOB":"Tans gewild op Bing","LOC_HOMEPAGE_BELOW_SEARCHBOX_TOB":"Tans gewild op Bing","LOC_HOMEPAGE_BELOW_SEARCHBOX_TOB_NEXT":"Volgende","LOC_HOMEPAGE_BELOW_S